 "text": "Government | Eaton County, MI\nSkip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\".\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nWelcome To Eaton County\nSearch\nGovernment\nDepartments\nHow Do I...\nHome\nGovernment\nGovernment\n9\n1\n1\n2\nAgendas & Minutes\nAccess easily searchable meeting agendas and minutes for various boards, commissions, and committees.\nBoard of Commissioners\nLearn about the role of the Board of Commissioners.\nBoards & Commissions\nBrowse a listing of commissions and subcommittees at Eaton County.\nEaton County Dashboard & Citizens Guide\nThe County is publishing on its website a performance measurement dashboard that monitors performance trends in several key areas. View related reports and other information.\nElected Officials\nEaton County elected officials manage the well being and welfare of our communities keeping the County running efficiently.\nElections\nView information issued from the County Clerk's Office about voter information, filing deadlines, upcoming elections and current election results in Eaton County.\nHistory of Eaton County\nRead about the history of Eaton County and view photos of historic landmarks.\nLocal Community Information\nAccess links to the websites for local communities, schools, police departments and fire agencies.\nAgendas & Minutes\nBoard of Commissioners\nCommittee Assignments\nPublic Safety Committee\nPublic Works & Human Services Committee\nWays & Means Committee\nMembers\nAndy Shaver - District 1\nChris Arndt - District 2\nJason Peek - District 3\nBrandon Haskell - District 4\nJeanne Pearl-Wright - District 5\nJane M.